-- title:
--   Pole clearing for functions regular on a strict first-kind disc
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ (an algebraic closure of $\mathbb Q$), a nonzero $N$, an algebraically closed field $k$ of characteristic $q$, a ring homomorphism $\mathrm{red} : A \to k$, a `ModularPolynomialData q` called `data` satisfying the Kronecker congruence `hKr` (its bivariate reduction mod $q$ equals $(C(X)^q - X)(C(X) - X^q)$), and witnesses `hα`, `hβ` that the two degeneracy embeddings `heckeAlphaBar`, `heckeBetaBar` of the base-changed modular function field of level $N$ into that of level $Nq$ are integral; let $P$ be a `PlaceSpecialization` for these data, so in particular a map `P.sp` from places of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-modular function field of level $N$ to places of `modularFunctionFieldC k N` compatible with the orders of vanishing of $j$ and $j_N$ under $\mathrm{red}$. Assume $q \nmid N$ and that $\mathrm{red}\,c = 0$ exactly for $c$ in the maximal ideal of $A$. Let $Q$ be a place of `modularFunctionFieldBar (N * q)` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ and write $\bar v =$ `P.reduceFst Q` for the specialisation of the restriction of $Q$ along `heckeAlphaBar`. Assume: `P.IsStrictFst Q`, i.e. geometric Frobenius carries $\bar v$ to `P.reduceSnd Q` while its square does not fix $\bar v$; there is a pair $c \in k \times k$ which is a centre of $\bar v$ (both $\mathrm{ord}_{\bar v}(j^{\mathrm{geom}} - c_1)$ and $\mathrm{ord}_{\bar v}(j_N^{\mathrm{geom}} - c_2)$ are positive) and $\bar v$ is the only place of `modularFunctionFieldC k N` with centre $c$; and $\bar v(j_N^{\mathrm{geom}})^{q^2} \neq \bar v(j_N^{\mathrm{geom}})$ for the residue evaluation. Let $z, y_1, y_2$ lie in `modularFunctionFieldBar (N * q)`, let $u \in A$ and $w : \mathrm{Fin}\,2 \to A$, and assume `IsFstTriple` holds for $\bar v$, the value $\mathrm{red}\,u$ and $(z, y_1, y_2)$: either $z = j$, $y_1 = j_N$, $y_2 = j_{Nq}$ with $\mathrm{ord}_{\bar v}(j^{\mathrm{geom}} - \mathrm{red}\,u) = 1$, or $z = j_N$, $y_1 = j$, $y_2 = j_{Nq}$ with $\mathrm{ord}_{\bar v}(j_N^{\mathrm{geom}} - \mathrm{red}\,u) = 1$. Assume further $\mathrm{ord}_Q(z - u) > 0$ and $\mathrm{ord}_Q(y_{j+1} - w_j) > 0$ for $j \in \mathrm{Fin}\,2$. Finally let $f$ be an element of `modularFunctionFieldBar (N * q)` lying in the valuation subring of every place $W$ with `P.IsStrictFst W` and `P.reduceFst W` $= \bar v$. Then there exists a polynomial $H$ over $A$ in the variables indexed by `Option (Fin 2)` such that $\mathrm{red}$ of the value of $H$ at $(u; w_0, w_1)$ is nonzero in $k$, and $f \cdot H(z; y_1, y_2)$, where $H$ is evaluated through $A \to \overline{\mathbb Q} \to$ `modularFunctionFieldBar (N * q)`, is integral over the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-subalgebra generated by the $j$-function `ProlongationTuple.jFun N q`.
--
--   This is the horizontal pole-clearing step for the modular curve of level $Nq$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$: a function regular at every strict first-kind place with the given first reduction is made integral over $\overline{\mathbb Q}[j]$ after multiplication by a polynomial expression in the coordinate triple which is a unit at the centre. It is used in establishing the model property `ProlongationTuple.IsModel`, where such a product is compared with values in the smooth local ring of the first reduction.
